        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          An infrared heater is an electric heater with a glowing quartz or carbon element that sends out radiant heat, the same kind you feel from the sun or a campfire. It warms the people, furniture and floor in its line of sight before it warms the air, which is why you feel it within seconds. What it does not do is make more heat from the same electricity. A 1,500-watt infrared heater, a 1,500-watt ceramic fan heater and a 1,500-watt oil-filled radiator all put out the same amount of heat, about 5,100 BTU an hour. So the right reason to buy infrared is comfort in a cold or drafty spot, not a lower bill. We picked seven infrared and quartz heaters with the safety features that matter and say plainly where each one fits.
        </p>

