          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Quartz Tower, Infrared Cabinet or Wall Panel: Pick the Type That Fits Your Room
          </h2>

          <p>
            Infrared heaters sold for homes come in four shapes, and the shape decides how much of the heat arrives as direct radiant warmth and how much as warm air from a fan. Pick the type for how you use the room, then pick the model.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Quartz Tube Towers: Fast, Direct Heat for One Person</h3>

          <p>
            A quartz tower has glowing quartz tubes behind a grille and a curved reflector that throws the heat forward. Many, like the BLACK+DECKER BHTI06, add a small fan. These are the most truly radiant of the group: aim one at your chair and you feel it right away. They are light, cheap and ideal for a desk or reading chair, but they warm what is in front of them and leave the back of the room cold.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Infrared Cabinet Heaters: Even Room Heat with a Fan</h3>

          <p>
            Cabinet heaters, such as the Dr. Infrared and Comfort Zone models below, put quartz elements inside a box and use a blower to push air across them and out through a front grille. Most of their heat leaves as warm air, so they behave more like a quiet fan heater than a campfire. That is a strength: they heat a whole room more evenly, and the elements are enclosed, which suits homes with children and pets.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Wall-Mounted Infrared Panels: Off the Floor</h3>

          <p>
            Wall-mount units, like the Heat Storm Phoenix, hang on the wall and keep floor space clear. They suit a bathroom-adjacent dressing area, a small office or a room with nowhere safe to set a heater on the floor. Check where your outlet is before you buy: the cord still has to reach a wall socket without an extension cord.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Infrared Fireplace Stoves: Heat with a Flame Effect</h3>

